description:
Compile and execute C# code in the Unity Editor.
The code runs on the Editor's main thread, so it can safely call any Unity API (UnityEngine, UnityEditor, etc.). Private and internal types, APIs, properties, events, constructors, and fields can be accessed directly without reflection when `enable_non_public_access` is enabled (the default).

Code without a top-level `await` runs inside a synchronous body. Code with a top-level `await` runs inside `public static async Task<object> ExecuteAsync(..., ExecuteCodeContext ctx, CancellationToken cancellationToken)`. Both use the same main-thread task entry; single-frame code runs to completion immediately, and long editor operations can split work across frames with `await ctx.wait`.

Common usings are pre-included: System, System.IO, System.Text, System.Linq, System.Reflection, System.Threading, System.Threading.Tasks, System.Collections, System.Collections.Generic, UnityEngine, UnityEngine.SceneManagement, UnityEngine.UI, UnityEditor, UnityEditor.SceneManagement, UnityEditor.Animations, Locus.

Locus auto-injects further `using` directives for common Unity/package namespaces and uniquely resolved project or package types. If a short type name is ambiguous, compilation fails and the error lists the candidate full type names; only then use a fully qualified name or an explicit top-level `using`.

Returning results to the agent:
- print(obj)       — append obj.ToString() to the result buffer (plain text, one line per call)
- printJson(obj)   — serialize to JSON and append. Uses EditorJsonUtility for UnityEngine.Object (full serialized fields), JsonUtility for plain C# objects. Preferred for structured data.
- clear()          — clear the result buffer
- Expression mode  — if the entire code is a single expression, its value is automatically printed.

Context API:
- `ctx.GetConsoleLog(level, limit)` reads the current Unity Console without reflection. `level` is optional (`error`, `warn`, or `info`), `limit` defaults to 50 and is capped at 200, and repeated entries are merged with a `count`. Use `printJson(ctx.GetConsoleLog("error", 50))` to return it.
- `await ctx.wait` / `await ctx.WaitFrame()` resumes on a later Editor update; `ctx.WaitFrames(int)`, `ctx.WaitSeconds(float)` and `ctx.WaitUntil(Func<bool>)` wait accordingly.
- `ctx.Progress(title, info, progress)` reports progress to the Locus tool call panel and returns true only if execution is already cancelled; `ctx.ClearProgress()` clears it; `ctx.ThrowIfCancellationRequested()` and `ctx.CancellationToken` handle cancellation.
- When `com.unity.test-framework` is installed, use `await UnityTestApi.ListAsync(query)` for discovery and `UnityTestApi.Start(options)`, `Status(runId)`, and `Cancel(runId)` for persisted test runs. These APIs call the official TestRunner directly.

For long loops, process a batch per frame, report progress, then `await ctx.wait`. Unity synchronous calls (SaveScene, AssetDatabase.SaveAssets, asset import) still run synchronously while called.

IMPORTANT:
- `request_editor_status` declares the required status before running. If the current status must change, or the code explicitly changes status through EditorApplication play/pause APIs, Locus applies the Unity status-change permission before continuing.
- Bare `return;` fails to compile — exit early with `return null;` (a trailing `return null;` is auto-appended, so explicit returns are usually unnecessary).
- Debug.Log / Debug.LogWarning / Debug.LogError write to the Unity Console. Read them with `unity_get_console_log` or `ctx.GetConsoleLog(...)`, and use print() or printJson() for the current execution result.
- Do NOT trigger script recompilation (e.g. CompilationPipeline.RequestScriptCompilation() or importing/modifying .cs files) — the Locus plugin would lose its Unity connection.

Examples:
```
// Batch edit with frame yields
var objects = UnityEngine.Object.FindObjectsOfType<GameObject>();
for (int i = 0; i < objects.Length; i++)
{
    objects[i].name = objects[i].name.Trim();
    if (i % 50 == 0)
    {
        ctx.Progress("Normalize names", $"{i}/{objects.Length}", i / (float)objects.Length);
        await ctx.wait;
    }
}
ctx.ClearProgress();
print($"normalized {objects.Length} objects");
```
```
// Read recent errors without UnityEditor.LogEntries reflection
printJson(ctx.GetConsoleLog("error", 50));
```
```
// Discover Edit Mode tests through the typed Locus API
var tests = await UnityTestApi.ListAsync(new UnityTestQuery { Mode = UnityTestMode.Edit });
printJson(tests);
```
```
// Single expression — value is auto-returned
Application.unityVersion
```
